Of nouls' 475 catalogue questions, 103 (22%) are about a family a deterministic zanity rule detects, so zanity answers them without a model. zanity asks no question per family.

# Speed

On an M3 Max whose endpoint security slows every file open by a binary Apple didn't sign, which taxes zanity and the Python tools alike.

```=html
<div class="headline">
<div><strong>2.3×</strong> faster on every rule, from an empty cache, than the fastest tool, mockbuster, on its own 6: 179 ms against 418 ms.</div>
<div><strong>2.5–7.3×</strong> faster than nasa-lsp, testdesiderata, mockbuster, dddlint, each on its own rules; bonsai, which rebuilds its index on every run, is 121× slower.</div>
</div>
```

